  "priorities": [
    "Keep all available weapons contributing; finish an accessible wounded enemy before spreading damage.",
    "Select at most one retreating Marine: among allies taking recent damage, choose lowest health fraction, then greatest recent health loss, then lowest ally index.",
    "That Marine retreats during cooldown only when a legal endpoint increases separation from threatening enemies without isolating it. Prefer proximity to the other allies; break endpoint ties by action ID.",
    "Other Marines maintain pressure. Rejoin fire once pressure drops; near the time limit, prioritize attacks and pursuit over repeated retreats."
  ],
  "contingencies": [
    "If the focus disappears, reassess visible targets; disappearance is not a confirmed kill. With no enemies visible, search together toward last observed contact, otherwise the center.",
    "If retreat offers no useful separation, attack rather than oscillate. If an action is rejected, select from current legal criteria; acceptance alone does not establish firing."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Apply this policy independently across episodes. Current observations override initial positions; no healing, abilities, upgrades, or hidden enemy state are assumed."
  ],
  "unit_roles": [
    {
      "unit_type": "Marine",
      "guidance": "Every Marine is a damage dealer. Healthier allies sustain the firing line while the single threatened ally briefly withdraws; roles change with observed damage and health."
    }
  ]
}"}}
